<title>FRANCE: Axa-UAP denies market rumour of DLJ sale.</title>
<headline>Axa-UAP denies market rumour of DLJ sale.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>French insurer Axa-UAP denied market rumours on Friday that it would like to sell U.S. bank Donaldson, Lufkin &amp; Jeanrette, a unit of Equitable Cos Inc.</p>
<p>&quot;This crops up frequently. We deny all talk of a sale of DLJ,&quot; a spokeswoman told Reuters.</p>
<p>The stock was little affected by the rumour which traders were citing. Axa-UAP shares were flat at 369.0 francs in a weaker market amid small volumes.</p>
<p>DLJ is 80 percent owned by Equitable, with 20 percent of its capital quoted on the New York stock exchange. Equitable is in turn 60 percent controlled by Axa-UAP.</p>
</text>
